      "id": 1,
      "text": "Blairsville sprang up in 1818 where the Northern Turnpike met the Conemaugh River, booming after the Pennsylvania Main Line Canal opened.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.indianacountypa.gov/indiana-county-communities/blairsville/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first Pennsylvania Railroad branch in Indiana County was built in Blairsville in 1851, turning the borough into a rail hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.indianacountypa.gov/indiana-county-communities/blairsville/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Peter’s Episcopal Church, built in 1830, and its rectory in Blairsville are listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
